{"title":"Concave polygon","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Concave_polygon.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/8b/Concave_polygon.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"316\" height=\"237\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>A <b>concave polygon</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">polygon</a> that has an \"opening\" in it. In other words, there are two points, A, and B, in the interior of the polgon such that a portion of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Segment\" title=\"Segment\">segment</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is not in the boundary of the polygon. A concave polygon has at least one <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Reflex_angle\" title=\"Reflex angle\">reflex angle</a>, or an angle that is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/0/3f0cd95f95238159d02dbcea0aca632c2928991c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Concave_polygon&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Convex_polygon\" title=\"Convex polygon\">Convex polygon</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Concave_polyhedron\" title=\"Concave polyhedron\">Concave polyhedron</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Concave_polygon&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017235407\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.020 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 22/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 286/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 364/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.465      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.465      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5328:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017235407 and revision id 21960. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}